Package: heb
Title: Hierarchical Empirical Bayes Batch Correction from Reference Samples
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
    person("M. D.", "Manurung", email = "m.d.manurung@lumc.nl", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates technical batch effects in cytometry data from
    repeated reference samples with a linear mixed model per population and
    marker: donor effects fixed, study and batch effects random, variance
    components by restricted maximum likelihood. The correction of a batch is
    the difference of its best linear unbiased prediction and that of an
    anchor batch. Models are frozen with a digest and applied to new data
    without changing earlier corrections. Ported from the 'heb' and
    'heb_shared' engines of SpectraWeaveR.
